    "Full API spec": "Module: twenty48.types\n- Direction: enum.Enum with members LEFT=auto, RIGHT=auto, UP=auto, DOWN=auto.\n- GameStatus: enum.Enum with members RUNNING=auto, WON=auto, LOST=auto.\nImport contract: Only absolute imports allowed from other modules (e.g., from twenty48.types import Direction, GameStatus).\n\nModule: twenty48.move\n- def move_line_left(line: list[int]) -> tuple[list[int], int]\n  Inputs:\n    - line: list of length <= 4 containing non-negative integers; zeros represent empty cells. If length < 4, it will be treated as given and padded in output to length 4.\n  Behavior:\n    - Implements the canonical 2048 merge for a single row moving left using this exact algorithm:\n      1) Create a compacted list by filtering out zeros from the input line (preserving order).\n      2) Initialize i = 0 and merge_score = 0.\n      3) While i < len(compacted) - 1:\n         - If compacted[i] == compacted[i+1]: set compacted[i] *= 2; set compacted[i+1] = 0; increment merge_score by compacted[i]; increment i by 2.\n         - Else: increment i by 1.\n      4) Create merged = [x for x in compacted if x != 0].\n      5) Pad merged with zeros on the right until length is exactly 4.\n    - No in-place pops are allowed; the function should use new lists for filtered/padded sequences.\n  Returns:\n    - (new_line, merge_score) where new_line is length 4 and merge_score is the sum of merged tile values produced in this move step.\n  Purity:\n    - Function is pure: no mutation of input list, no global state, no I/O.\n\nModule: twenty48.board\n- class Board:\n  - grid: list[list[int]] of shape 4x4; integers >= 0; 0 denotes empty.\n  - def get_grid(self) -> list[list[int]]\n    Returns a deep copy or safe-to-read copy of the 4x4 grid suitable for inspection in tests or by Game.\n  - def reset_empty(self) -> None\n    Sets grid to all zeros (4x4).\n  - def move(self, direction: Direction) -> tuple[bool, int]\n    Applies a move in the given direction to the board.\n    Uses twenty48.move.move_line_left on each row/column, transforming rows/columns as needed for RIGHT/UP/DOWN by reversing or transposing.\n    Returns (changed, gained_score) where changed is True if any tile moved or merged; gained_score is the total merge_score from all lines.\n  - def can_move(self) -> bool\n    Returns True if any cell is empty or any adjacent pair (horizontal or vertical) can merge.\n  - def has_target(self, target: int = 2048) -> bool\n    Returns True if any cell equals target.\n  - def empty_positions(self) -> list[tuple[int, int]]\n    Returns a list of (row, col) coordinates where grid[row][col] == 0, in row-major order.\n  - def add_random_tile(self, rng: random.Random) -> bool\n    If there are empty positions, selects one uniformly at random using rng.choice and places a tile: 2 with probability 0.9, else 4 with probability 0.1. Returns True if a tile was added, else False.\n  Notes:\n    - Board must not depend on Game; only depends on Direction and move_line_left.\n\nModule: twenty48.game\n- class Game:\n  - def __init__(self, seed: int = 0)\n    Initializes Game with a deterministic random.Random seeded with seed, a Board, score=0, and status=GameStatus.RUNNING.\n  - def reset(self) -> None\n    Resets the Board to empty, sets score=0, status=RUNNING, and spawns exactly two tiles using add_random_tile(self.rng) twice.\n  - def move(self, direction: Direction) -> bool\n    If status is not RUNNING, returns False and makes no changes.\n    Otherwise, applies Board.move(direction). If changed is True, increments score by gained_score, then:\n      - If board.has_target(2048), set status=WON.\n      - Else, call board.add_random_tile(self.rng). After spawning, if not board.can_move(), set status=LOST.\n    Returns changed.\n  - def get_status(self) -> GameStatus\n  - def get_score(self) -> int\n  - def get_board(self) -> Board\n  Import contract: May import only twenty48.board.Board, twenty48.types.Direction and GameStatus.\n\nModule: twenty48.__init__\n- Re-exports: Board, Game, Direction, GameStatus for convenience (from .board import Board, etc.). Must not introduce circular imports (place after concrete modules exist).\n\nModule: Main.py\n- def run_demo(seed: int) -> tuple[GameStatus, int, int]\n  Behavior:\n    - Create Game(seed), call reset().\n    - Perform exactly one move to Direction.LEFT.\n    - Compute tiles_count as the number of non-zero tiles on the board after the move (and possible spawn if the move changed).\n    - Return (status, score, tiles_count) where status is game.get_status(), score is game.get_score().\n  Notes:\n    - No printing, GUI, I/O, or networking. Absolute imports only: from twenty48.game import Game; from twenty48.types import Direction, GameStatus.\n\nCross-module import rules:\n- Only absolute imports within the twenty48 package hierarchy are allowed (e.g., from twenty48.move import move_line_left). No relative imports.\n- Dependency direction is acyclic: types -> move -> board -> game; __init__ re-exports only.\n- Main.py depends only on twenty48.game and twenty48.types.\n\nTest usage contract:\n- tests/test_main.py imports run_demo from Main and move_line_left from twenty48.move. Tests assert determinism and canonical move behavior. No other modules are imported in tests.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "Preserve protocol files exactly: requirements.txt, Main.py, tests/test_main.py. Main.py is a thin entry exposing run_demo(seed) and performing a single left move on a deterministic Game. The 2048 core resides in a snake_case package twenty48 with modules: types.py (Direction, GameStatus enums), move.py (pure move_line_left), board.py (Board 4x4 grid; movement via move_line_left; spawn and availability checks), game.py (seeded RNG orchestration; reset with two spawns; scoring; win/loss transitions). Enforce absolute imports within twenty48.* and no GUI/I/O/network. Tests are headless and deterministic: validate move_line_left fixtures and smoke test run_demo(0).",
    "Execution Protocol": "Run pytest. There is exactly one protocol-level test file: tests/test_main.py. The runtime entry is Main.py exposing run_demo(seed). Tests must be headless, make no GUI/I/O calls, and rely on deterministic seeded RNG. Do not add/rename protocol files.",
